<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16707" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστυ-νόμος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέμω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>protecting the city,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					88
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλαΐαι ἀ.</span>
			<i>public</i> festivals, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				9.31
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργαὶ ἀ.</span> the feelings
				<i>of law-abiding</i> or <i>social life,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				355
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., <i>a magistrate who had the care of the
				police, streets, and public buildings</i> at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				1.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				50.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				313.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				25a
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>: in other cities, as Tenos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).883.14
			</span></i>; Iasos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				169.10
			</span></i>; Rhodes, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(1).1
			</span></i>; Pergamum, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				483.7
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				759a
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			= Lat. <i>praetor urbanus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				53.2
			</span></i>.</div>
